The period of the contrast variation (the distance in mirror movement that causes the next zero) is the change in OPD for the next minimum, which is $\Delta \Delta = \frac{\lambda^2_{\text{avg}}}{\Delta \lambda}$. Given that the mirror is moved by 0.44 mm, the corresponding OPD change is $2 \times 0.44 \text{ mm} = 0.88 \text{ mm}$. This OPD period should equal $\frac{\lambda^2_{\text{avg}}}{\Delta \lambda}$.

